Whoa! End screen is transparent, and world remains visible with enemies; the overlay appears semi-transparent? In previous victory screenshot it was dark and clean. Here it looks ghostly transparent because we called updateGame 6000 times without letting browser paint / CSS animations? End overlay has background maybe semi-transparent + overlay-grain with animation? Screenshot captured immediately after evaluate returns, perhaps CSS opacity transition not completed, so overlay is fading in from 0. `end-screen` may have animation fade. In previous test we waited 3s. Here screenshot immediately, so overlay at start of fade. Not a bug. Fine.

But there is a bigger issue in this screenshot: at top right a huge cluster of enemies and pickups, because player invincible and stationary at end? It's fine.

Now gold sink implementation. Let's inspect sheet-foot and header layout, plus CSS for buttons disabled. We'll add a mend button in inventory header. But current gold pill at header; add button next to gold.

HTML:
```
<div class="gold-pill">...</div>
<button id="mend-btn" class="btn btn-small btn-ghost">Mend · 30g</button>
```
Order maybe before gold.

JS ui:
- ui.mendBtn = $("mend-btn")
- init listener: const r=actions.mendWounds(); renderInventory(); showToast...
- renderInventory update mend button state: `ui.mendBtn.textContent = \`Mend 35% · ${MEND_COST}g\`; disabled = hp>=max || gold<cost;`
Need share MEND_COST. Could define in engine and import? Better define `export const MEND_COST = 30;` in loot.js? Not loot. Put in state.js constants. Add `MEND_COST`, `reforgeCost(item)` in loot.js. UI imports MEND_COST from state. Engine imports reforgeCost. Simpler hardcode 30 in both with constant in loot.js and import ui from loot? ui already imports from loot. Export `MEND_COST` from loot.js and import in ui. But engine imports from loot too. Fine.

- Engine mendWounds:
```
