 sound...
 showToast(...)
 return true
}
```
Should preserve name/flavor (item identity) but if weapon style same, fine. New item's `power` is randomized. This is a reroll. For legendary, since powerDef same? createItem picks random legendaryPower; should reassign item.legendaryPower = fresh.legendaryPower. Then legendary power can change, fun. But name might no longer match power, not important. For consistency, maybe also `item.legendaryPower = fresh.legendaryPower`. Yes. Need ensure item.color etc unchanged.

- Compare/reforge with equipped: recalcStats.

- Detail action row: both sources show equip/salvage or unequip; add reforge button. For source bag, currently actions: Equip, Salvage. Add Reforge would be 3 buttons cramped. Could add below: full row. Use `<div class="item-actions">...` then `<button class="btn btn-ghost btn-small btn-reforge" data-action="reforge">Reforge ...</button>` in a second div. Or replace salvage? No. Add 3rd small button; pane width 348, buttons each ~100, okay. Text "Reforge 78g" ~ fits. We'll add to same row, CSS flex:1. For equipped source, "Unequip" + "Reforge". Good.

- UI handler for `reforge`: call actions.reforge(item); renderInventory().

- If reforge changes equipped weapon min/max etc, update HUD.

- After reforge, selection same object id; renderInventory fine.

Also add MEND_COST to loot export, reforgeCost.

Let's add HTML button.

